	(descr "HanRun HR911105A RJ45 with magnetics and LEDs, horizontal THT. Source: HanRun mechanical drawing 'Comp Side View' as reproduced in the Handsontec HR911105A data spec p.2 (https://handsontec.com/dataspecs/connector/RJ-45%20Ethernet-2.pdf ; HanRun's own PDF not reachable: datasheet.lcsc.com serves HTML), cross-checked against KiCad's Connector_RJ RJ45_Hanrun_HR911105A at 7ebfa6b2 (same hole set, pin 1 origin): 3.25 NPTH 11.43 apart; shield 1.63 holes 15.49 apart, 3.05 behind the NPTH line; signal pins 0.89 holes, 1.27 stagger, 2.54 pitch per row, pins 1/3/5/7 6.35 and 2/4/6/8 8.89 behind the NPTH line; LED pins 1.02 holes, 13.25 / 11.43 spans, 4.90 in front of it. Body 16.00 x 21.40, front face 10.92 in front of the NPTH line. Pad map (p.3): 1 TD+, 2 TD-, 3 RD+, 4 TX CT, 5 RX CT, 6 RD-, 7 NC, 8 CHS GND, 9/10 green LED A/K, 12/11 yellow LED A/K, 13/14 shield. Origin: mating axis on the NPTH line (panel centre). Corrected 2026-11-14 (audio-reproduction-systems boards/footprint-checks-2026-11-14.md): the 2026-11-09 copy had the signal rows 2.54 mm too far back (8.89 / 11.43) and the LED row at 3.05 instead of 4.90.")
